EXPERIMENT 19 – SIMULATING USER THINK TIME USING CONSTANT TIMER IN APACHE JMETER

AIM
To use Apache JMeter to simulate user think time using the Constant Timer.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and create a Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Set Number of Threads = 5, Ramp-up Period = 5 seconds and Loop Count = 3.
4. Add an HTTP Request sampler for the home page (GET /).
5. Add a Constant Timer and set Thread Delay = 2000 milliseconds.
6. Run the plan with the timer enabled.
7. Disable the timer and run the plan again.
8. Compare the throughput of both runs.
TEST PLAN CONFIGURATION
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Number of Threads	5
Thread Group	Ramp-up Period	5 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	3
HTTP Request	Protocol	https
HTTP Request	Server Name	the-internet.herokuapp.com
HTTP Request	Method / Path	GET /
Constant Timer	Thread Delay	2000 milliseconds

INPUT
- Number of users: 5
- Loop count: 3
- Timer delay: 2000 milliseconds (2 seconds)
- Total samples: \(5 \times 3 = 15\)
OUTPUT
Summary Report (Timer Enabled)
Label	Samples	Error %	Throughput
Home Page	15	0.00%	Lower value/sec

Summary Report (Timer Disabled)
Label	Samples	Error %	Throughput
Home Page	15	0.00%	Higher value/sec

Throughput values depend on the system and network.
RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to simulate user think time using the Constant Timer, and the results were verified.
